# Build output is COMMITTED on purpose.
#
# Consumers install this package straight from a git URL, and package managers
# differ on whether they run a dependency's `prepare` script: npm does, but bun
# blocks dependency lifecycle scripts unless the user opts in with
# `bun pm trust`. If build/ were gitignored, `main: build/index.js` would fail
# to resolve on bun and the package would be unusable.
#
# To change the sources:
#   1. edit src/
#   2. npm run build      (or: bun run build)
#   3. commit both src/ and build/ together
#
# (the rule itself lives at the bottom of this file, commented out)

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Xcode
#
ios/build/
*.pbxuser
!default.pbxuser
*.mode1v3
!default.mode1v3
*.mode2v3
!default.mode2v3
*.perspectivev3
!default.perspectivev3
xcuserdata
*.xccheckout
*.moved-aside
DerivedData
*.hmap
*.ipa
*.xcuserstate
project.xcworkspace

# Android / IntelliJ
#
android/build/
android/.cxx/
android/.gradle/
.classpath
.idea
*.iml
local.properties
android/app/libs
android/keystores/debug.keystore

# CocoaPods
example/ios/Pods
example/vendor/

# Lockfile: this is a library, not an app. Consumers resolve it.
bun.lock
bun.lockb
package-lock.json
yarn.lock

# Misc
.DS_Store
.vscode/
jsconfig.json
npm-debug.log
yarn-debug.log
